ho is going to be affected by cloudcover?replyaljgz 55 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Living in Vancouver, I traveled to Toronto to watch the Eclipse in 2024. We faced a nasty cloud, and had to drive hundreds of kilometers (hundreds of miles) to get a reasonably good view. On the drive back I decided that I'll travel for the one that's happening today, and here I am, in Sierra, with some cool people.Solar eclipses happen rarely enough, and frequently enough, to act as milestones in my life: I can review what happened since the previous one, and make a plan for the next one.They are some of the most magnificent natural phenomena, much more interesting than what's expected.The only other one that I got to see in perfect conditions was in my home town, Isfahan in 1999. I hope this one is perfectly clear again, and I have some resolutions for the next one.replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] This is great, can easily see what spots are overfilled with people or not :) I'm still thinking about where exactly I'll go to see it, was thinking Calafell or Vilanova as they're nearby and easily accessible, but probably half of Barcelona thinks the same so better to go a bit inland. Probably I'll end up just outside Lleida I think.Any more Spanish HNers (or temporary visitors) who are going to any specific places to see it? :)replyAl-Khwarizmi 57 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm from A Coruña so I should be able to just go down to the street, walk like 100 m and see it. I just hope clouds don't spoil the show (at the moment it's looking good, but here you never know).replyegesko 46 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'm in Valencia, planning to watch it from the beach.replyiancuandrei 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'll go somewhere around Bilbaoreplydavidricodias 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Colmenar Viejo seems a great spot ;)replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | root | parent | next [–] Only 7 hours away :D I'm in the Maresme area, so probably will end up between València and Tarragona on some mountain :) Thanks for the tip though, I'll forward it to my Madrid friends.replyhagen8 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Mountains close to leon?replygillesjacobs 31 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Cool, there is no check on the direction of the camera. Various camera's I checked do not seem to point in the direction of the sun during totality. It does filter candidate cameras down though.replyLongwelwind 26 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Does anyone know if there will be any live feed of the earth viewed from space during the eclipse?replyHelloUsername 9 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Maybe here? https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rSvCuSQhC3wreplyLawrenceKerr 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Doesn't seem like the best of weather now in Iceland, hopefully it clears up. Otherwise it would suck for the people who have planned the trip months if not years in advance only to get a clouded sky, but that's always the risk with astrotravel.replybenoliver999 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] Surely the smart money is to go to Spainreplyembedding-shape 58 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] We do get cloudy days too sometimes :) Although today it is looking fairly sunny all over the place: https://i.imgur.com/4LK7xo8.pngreplyIAmGraydon 3 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Ugh - I didn't know this will pass over Reykjavik. Would have been fantastic to see from there.replyTornhoof 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Sierra de Guadarrama - Puerto de Cotos https://www.infonieve.es/espacio-nordico/puerto-de-cotos/web... looks decent, different views, good weather.replyxanthine 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Sorry for my ignorance, but can someone please explain what I'm looking at here?replymsdz 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] About five hours from now, the sections of Europe indicated on the map will experience a total solar eclipse, with other regions of the continent experiencing a partial one.The map shows feeds to watch it.replyembedding-shape 