celona thinks the same so better to go a bit inland. Probably I'll end up just outside Lleida I think.Any more Spanish HNers (or temporary visitors) who are going to any specific places to see it? :)replyAl-Khwarizmi 57 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm from A Coruña so I should be able to just go down to the street, walk like 100 m and see it. I just hope clouds don't spoil the show (at the moment it's looking good, but here you never know).replyegesko 46 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'm in Valencia, planning to watch it from the beach.replyiancuandrei 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'll go somewhere around Bilbaoreplydavidricodias 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Colmenar Viejo seems a great spot ;)replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | root | parent | next [–] Only 7 hours away :D I'm in the Maresme area, so probably will end up between València and Tarragona on some mountain :) Thanks for the tip though, I'll forward it to my Madrid friends.replyhagen8 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Mountains close to leon?replygillesjacobs 31 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Cool, there is no check on the direction of the camera. Various camera's I checked do not seem to point in the direction of the sun during totality. It does filter candidate cameras down though.replyLongwelwind 26 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Does anyone know if there will be any live feed of the earth viewed from space during the eclipse?replyHelloUsername 9 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Maybe here? https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rSvCuSQhC3wreplyLawrenceKerr 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Doesn't seem like the best of weather now in Iceland, hopefully it clears up. Otherwise it would suck for the people who have planned the trip months if not years in advance only to get a clouded sky, but that's always the risk with astrotravel.replybenoliver999 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] Surely the smart money is to go to Spainreplyembedding-shape 58 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] We 